  "title": "Breaking: AlloyDB Instance Observability & Query Insights Properties Are Now Read-Only",
  "summary": "AlloyDB instances now expose `observabilityInstanceInfo` and `queryInsightsInfo` as output-only fields. Any existing code attempting to modify these properties will now encounter errors, as they are strictly immutable. Update your integrations to treat these as informational.",
  "details": "The `Instance` schema has been updated with two new top-level properties: `observabilityInstanceInfo` and `queryInsightsInfo`. These provide detailed, effective settings for observability and Query Insights features on your AlloyDB instances. Crucially, these properties, along with all their sub-fields (e.g., `ObservabilityInstanceInfo.enabled`, `QueryInsightsInstanceInfo.queryPlansPerMinute`), have been explicitly marked as read-only. This means any API calls attempting to set or update these values will now fail. Developers should update their code to treat these fields as informational output only.",
  "impact": "high",
  "breaking": true,
